<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1569" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Āgis</span></b> , ĭdis
		(acc. Agin, <i><span class="en">Cic. Off. 2, 23, 80</span></i>), m., =
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἀγις</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A king of Sparta</i>, <i>murdered by
				his own subjects</i>, <i><span class="en">Cic. Off.
				2, 23, 80</span></i>; cf. Plut. Agis.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>Brother of Agesilaus and son of Archidamus</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Nep. Ages. 1,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Lycian</i>, <i><span class="en">Verg. A.
				10, 751</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
